A||||2||ponya||Bumper reflectors||||5||
Z||000000||ponya||10-10-2000||06:02 AM||||I am in the process of re-finishing the front and rear bumper covers. Can the recessed reflectors be removed without removing the bumper? I could tape them up, but it would be much neater removing and then replacing them.Any info appreciated,   Thanks  Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tigger||10-10-2000||08:44 AM||||The reflectors in the rear bumper have two posts each that go thru the bumper and are held in by two sheet metal press on washers.<P>Removing them would be well worth it and give you a neater paint job for sure.<P>Personally I'd remove the bumper, but you don't want to completely remove the bumper then, try removing the the lower plastic pull rivets that hold the bottom side of the bumper to the subframe, the side marker lights to get access to the screws that hold the side of the bumper on the sides, then pull the bumper back so you can get to the backside of those reflectors and remove the clips.  At this point tho, all you'd have to do is remove the taillights, remove the pull rivets along the topside of the bumper and turn and remove the license plate lights to completely remove the bumper cover.<P><BR>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-10-2000||04:14 PM||||Get some extra plastic rivets, they seem to break when you are removing them.||||reg||3
